    # v378 (30/09/2026, night), operator orders: «tem alguma coisa que deixamos passar, examine por favor» (is there something we missed? examine it); «concordo prossiga» (I agree, proceed)
    _c8 = core.get("the_dissipation_law_with_contrast_v378") or {}; _w8 = core.get("what_was_missed_v378") or {}; _b8 = core.get("bancada_fase4_v378") or {}
    _v8 = lambda d_: str(d_.get("verdict", "n/a")).replace("_", r"\_")
    _nv8 = lambda d_, t_: "" if d_.get("all_verified") is True else (r"\textbf{In this run %s did NOT close: what follows is the statement, not a seal.} " % t_)
    _f8 = lambda x_, n_=2: (("%%.%df" % n_) % float(x_)) if isinstance(x_, (int, float)) else "n/a"
    _tx8 = lambda k_, d_="n/a": str(k_ if k_ is not None else d_).replace("_", r"\_")
    _P8 = _b8.get("P_ladder_d1b") or {}; _T8 = _b8.get("T_intermediate_d1b") or {}; _S8 = _b8.get("S_joint_d1b") or {}; _K8 = _b8.get("stacked_control") or {}; _sh8 = _w8.get("shadow_readers_planck_lcdm_D1b") or {}
    _lnP8 = _P8.get("lnB") or {}; _lnT8 = _T8.get("lnB") or {}; _pT8 = _b8.get("posterior_T") or {}
    s.append(r"\paragraph*{Beside (v378) --- What was missed: the derived kernel D1b and the double-counting reading of $\bTGL$; the dissipation law with contrast; Phase 4, the deviation.} "
             + _nv8(_c8, "the law with contrast") + _nv8(_w8, "what was missed") + _nv8(_b8, "Phase 4") +
             r"\textbf{(E12) Reading beside the v377 paragraph and Phases 2--3:} article 1 (\emph{Haja Luz}) has \emph{two} kernels for the flow law $d\ln H/dN=\bTGL\,\mathcal W$: D1a ($\mathcal W=1$, the v377 stone) and D1b, "
             r"the kernel \emph{derived} from continuity ($\mathcal W=|1+w_{\rm eff}|$); article 1 computes it ($0.034\sigma$), but the Bench had only tested D1a. And article 1 transports through the law the $\Lambda$CDM calibration of Planck, whereas Phases 2--3 applied the law on the TGL background of the effective map, "
             r"which already carries $\bTGL$ (the map $R\sqrt{1+\bTGL}$ and the E1 layer): the numbers differ by convention. The \emph{double counting} reading is the management's under the article's convention (\textsf{[DERIVED]} from the convention, not measured): article 1 itself treats the E1 layer and the law as distinct, coexisting hypotheses, and the effective map was ratified by the operator --- "
             r"which background is the background remains his decision \textsf{[OPEN]}. The v377 numbers stay; the reading stays beside. In the article's convention, with D1b, the six shadow readers sit $" + _f8(_sh8.get("z_comb")) + r"\sigma$ from the law "
             r"(reanalysis declared \emph{not blind}, read by hash); with the stacked background, $" + _f8(_w8.get("stacked_control_D1b_z")) + r"\sigma$. Verdict: \texttt{" + _v8(_w8) + r"}.")
    s.append(r"\emph{The dissipation law with contrast} (\texttt{TGLExt.TheFlowLawContrast}): the same leak family $t\mapsto e^{-t\bTGL g}$, read with the \emph{mean} contrast over the register, implies "
             r"$H_0^{\mathrm{local}}=H_0^{\mathrm{bg}}\exp\!\big(\bTGL\int_0^{N}g\big)$; $g\equiv1$ recovers the v377 stone (D1a is the particular case); $\bTGL=0$ recovers $\Lambda$CDM; $\int g>0$ implies local $>$ background. "
             r"For the flat-FRW contrast, $g=\tfrac23\,d\ln E/dN$, the signed derivative (\textsf{[KNOWN]}: Raychaudhuri; the identification with $|1+w_{\rm eff}|$ assumes $\rho+p\ge0$, a condition stated in the stone's prose, not a hypothesis of the theorems, and measured on the grid: $\min(1+w_{\rm eff})=" + _f8(_c8.get("min_1_plus_w_eff_grid"), 3) + r"$), "
             r"the fundamental theorem of calculus gives the closed form $\int_0^{N}g=\tfrac23\ln E(N)$ and the factor \textbf{$K=E(z_*)^{2\bTGL/3}$}: this run, with the Bench's Planck 2018 $\Lambda$CDM background (\textsf{[INPUT]}, not the literals of article 1), $I_b=" + _f8(_c8.get("I_b_closed_form"), 4) + r"$ nats against $N_*=" + _f8(_c8.get("register_N_star_nats"), 4)
             + r"$, $K_{\rm D1b}=" + _f8(_c8.get("K_D1b_runtime"), 6) + r"$ against $K_{\rm D1a}=" + _f8(_c8.get("K_D1a_runtime"), 6) + r"$; and \emph{the deviation reads below the asymptote}: $\int_0^{N}g\le N$ implies $\bTGL\,\bar g\le\bTGL$, with the deviation $\delta/\bTGL=\bar g-1=" + _f8(_c8.get("predicted_deviation_over_beta_D1b"), 4)
             + r"$ fixed by the background, with no free parameter. What nature decides stays with the observer: proved $\neq$ confirmed. Verdict: \texttt{" + _v8(_c8) + r"}.")
    s.append(r"\emph{Phase 4 of the Bench (30/09, night), pre-registered and read by hash} --- the deviation $\delta=\hat\beta-\bTGL$ in the article's convention ($\bTGL$ only in the law; $\Lambda$CDM background fitted to compressed Planck $+$ BAO), kernel D1b, with $\bTGL$ as the asymptote and the approach function fixed by the derived kernel: "
             r"\textbf{the ladder} (the whole register) reads $\delta=" + _f8(_P8.get("delta"), 5) + r"\pm" + _f8(_P8.get("sigma_delta"), 5) + r"$ per nat ($" + _f8(_P8.get("z_delta")) + r"\sigma$), pull $" + _f8(_P8.get("pull")) + r"\sigma$ at $\bTGL=\alpha\sqrt e$ (against $-4\sigma$ in $\Lambda$CDM), $\ln B(\mathrm{TGL}/\Lambda\mathrm{CDM})=" + _f8(_lnP8.get("tgl_vs_lcdm"))
             + r"$ (circularity declared in the pre-registration: the ladder and the calibration were already known when the law was coined; family P tests consistency, parsimony and replication, not the discovery of the law; the new incidence is family T); "
             r"\textbf{the intermediate registers} (the 32 Moresco$+$2022 chronometers, imported from article 1 and read with the accumulated law from $z_*$ down to $z$, as in C.5b --- the test that could lose, prior power $" + _f8(_b8.get("power_prior_cc_sigma")) + r"\sigma$; the direction already seen in the smoke test, declared under \emph{seen before}): $\delta=" + _f8(_T8.get("delta"), 5) + r"\pm" + _f8(_T8.get("sigma_delta"), 5)
             + r"$ ($" + _f8(_T8.get("z_delta")) + r"\sigma$ from $\bTGL$; $P(\beta>0)=" + _f8(_pT8.get("fracao_beta_acima_de_zero")) + r"$: consistent with $\beta=0$), law gain $" + _f8(_T8.get("z_ganho_da_lei")) + r"\sigma$, $\ln B=" + _f8(_lnT8.get("tgl_vs_lcdm")) + r"$ --- the intermediate clocks \emph{disfavour} the accumulated-flow reading at $\bTGL$ (diagonal errors: the significance is overstated); ladder $+$ chronometers jointly $" + _f8(_S8.get("z_delta")) + r"\sigma$; stacked control $" + _f8(_K8.get("z_delta")) + r"\sigma$. "
             r"Pre-registered verdicts: \texttt{" + _tx8(_b8.get("veredito_fase4")) + r"} and \texttt{" + _tx8(_b8.get("veredito_T")) + r"}. Reading \textsf{[OPEN/ONTO --- the management's, not adopted]}: if the intermediate clocks do not read the factor and the shadow does, only the shadow (the local distance readers) reads the leak and the clocks read the face; the inverse reading (the law is wrong) is equally admissible on these data; "
             r"which background is the background, and the form of the E1 layer, are the operator's decisions. Nothing here confirms ($\mathrm{NOT\_FALSIFIED}\neq\mathrm{CONFIRMED}$; GR is the classical limit). Module: \texttt{" + _v8(_b8) + r"}.")
